    "shop_smart":  [
                       "The three color bell pepper bag is cheaper than buying red and green loose, and fajitas want the mix anyway, so nothing is wasted.",
                       "One small can of chipotles in adobo seasons several batches. Freeze the leftover peppers in a flat bag and snap off what you need.",
                       "Refried beans in the can are the cheapest way to add body to a wrap. Buy the fat free version and season it yourself.",
                       "Reduced fat mozzarella melts creamy for fewer calories than full fat, and the bag freezes well if you only use a handful here."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Slice the chicken breast into strips and toss with the fajita seasoning and salt.",
                    "Warm the vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium high heat and cook the chicken strips until browned, then push them to one side.",
                    "Add the sliced green and red bell peppers and onion to the pan and cook 6 to 8 minutes until they take on color and soften, then drizzle in the honey and toss.",
                    "Warm the refried beans in a small pot until spreadable.",
                    "Stir the Greek yogurt, chipotle in adobo and reduced fat mozzarella into the hot chicken and peppers so the cheese melts and the sauce turns creamy and smoky.",
                    "Weigh the filling, subtract the empty bowl, and divide by 14. Spread refried beans down each tortilla, add a share of the creamy fajita filling, fold in the sides and roll.",
                    "Wrap each burrito and portion into 14 containers."
                ],
